'Xiangliu’s blood poisons the earth. Yu the Great beat him not just with strength but by controlling the water: drain the floods and the nine heads lose their power.':'相柳の血は大地を毒する。大禹は力だけでなく、水を治めて相柳を打ち負かした。洪水を引かせれば、九つの頭は力を失う。',
'Oni are the great demons of Japan: huge, with red or blue skin, horns, tusks, tiger-skin loincloths and iron clubs. They live on lonely mountains and islands and in the underworld, where they punish sinners. In the famous tale, Momotarō, the Peach Boy, sails to Onigashima, the island of the oni, with a dog, a monkey and a pheasant, defeats the demons and brings their treasure home.':'鬼は日本の大妖怪だ。巨大な体に赤や青の肌、角、牙、虎皮の腰布をまとい、鉄の棍棒を持つ。人里離れた山や島、そして罪人を罰する冥界に住む。名高い昔話では、桃太郎が犬、猿、雉を連れて鬼ヶ島へ渡り、鬼を倒して宝を持ち帰る。',
