'Every February at Setsubun, Japanese families throw roasted soybeans out of the door shouting ‘Oni wa soto! Fuku wa uchi!’ (‘Demons out! Luck in!’). Oni also hate holly leaves and the smell of grilled sardine heads.':'每年二月的节分，日本家庭会把炒黄豆撒向门外，高喊“鬼は外、福は内！”（“鬼出去，福进来！”）。鬼也讨厌冬青叶和烤沙丁鱼头的气味。',
'The kappa is a river imp the size of a child, with a turtle shell, webbed hands, a beak and a dish-shaped hollow on top of its head filled with water. It pulls horses and children into rivers to drown them and loves cucumbers above all things. Yet kappa also keep their promises: many tales tell of a defeated kappa teaching a family the secret of setting broken bones.':'河童是住在河里的小妖怪，身形如孩童，背有龟壳，手脚有蹼，长着鸟喙，头顶的碟状凹处盛着水。它会把马和孩子拖入河中淹死，最爱黄瓜。但河童也信守承诺：许多故事里，被打败的河童会教人家接骨的秘术。',
