addLang('ja', {
'The mangas is the great many-headed demon of Mongol and Buryat epics, a cannibal giant with twelve, fifteen or even a hundred heads. He devours whole herds and peoples and steals the wives of heroes. The hero Geser Khan and many epic warriors spend years hunting mangas, who split their souls into animals and objects hidden around the world.':'マンガスはモンゴルやブリヤートの叙事詩に登場する多頭の大悪魔で、十二、十五、時には百もの頭を持つ人食い巨人だ。家畜や人々を丸ごと食べ、英雄の妻をさらう。英雄ゲセル・ハーンや多くの戦士が長年追い求めるが、マンガスは魂を分け、世界各地の動物や物に隠している。',
'A mangas keeps its souls outside its body: in a fish, a bird, a golden box or a wasp. The hero must find and kill every soul, or the demon will rise again.':'マンガスは魂を体の外、魚や鳥、金の箱、蜂などに隠す。英雄はすべての魂を見つけて滅ぼさなければならない。さもなくば悪魔は復活する。',
'The olgoi-khorkhoi, the ‘large intestine worm’, is said to live under the sands of the Gobi desert. It is dark red, as thick as a man’s arm and up to a metre and a half long. Nomads say it can spit acid that eats through metal and kill from a distance with a blast like lightning. It comes out in June and July, after rain, when the ground is wet. Many expeditions have searched for it; none has found it.':'オルゴイ・コルホイは「大腸虫」を意味し、ゴビ砂漠の砂の下に住むという。濃い赤色で腕ほどの太さ、長さは一・五メートルにもなる。金属を溶かす酸を吐き、稲妻のような一撃で遠くの獲物を殺すと遊牧民は語る。地面が濡れる雨季の六月、七月に現れる。多くの探検隊が探したが、誰も発見していない。',
'Herders say the death worm is drawn to the colour yellow and that it hates the vibrations of footsteps. Stay off the dunes after summer rain.':'牧畜民によれば、死の虫は黄色に引き寄せられ、足音の振動を嫌う。夏の雨の後は砂丘に近づくな。',
'The Chimera was a fire-breathing monster of Lycia, with the body and head of a lion, a goat’s head rising from its back, and a snake for a tail. It burned the land and ate the flocks. King Iobates sent the young hero Bellerophon to kill it, hoping he would die. But Bellerophon tamed the winged horse Pegasus, flew above the Chimera, and pushed a lump of lead on the end of his spear into its fiery mouth. The lead melted and choked it.':'キマイラはリュキアの火を吐く怪物で、ライオンの頭と体、背中から生えた山羊の頭、蛇の尾を持つ。土地を焼き、家畜を食べた。イオバテス王は若き英雄ベレロポーンに退治を命じたが、死ぬことを期待していた。ベレロポーンは翼ある馬ペガサスを手なずけて怪物の上空を飛び、槍先の鉛塊を炎の口に押し込んだ。鉛が溶けて喉を塞ぎ、怪物は窒息した。',
'Attack from the air, where its three heads cannot reach you, and use its own fire against it: lead melted in its throat is what killed it.':'三つの頭が届かない空から攻め、自らの炎を逆手に取ろう。喉で溶けた鉛がキマイラを倒した。',
'Scylla was a monster with six long necks, each with a head full of three rows of sharp teeth, and dogs’ heads around her waist. She lived in a cave in the cliffs of a narrow strait, opposite the whirlpool Charybdis. Sailors had to choose between them. Odysseus chose to pass close to Scylla, losing six men, one for each head, rather than risk losing his whole ship to the whirlpool. Some said she was once a beautiful nymph, changed by a witch’s jealousy.':'スキュラは六本の長い首を持つ怪物で、各頭には鋭い歯が三列並び、腰の周りには犬の頭があった。狭い海峡の崖の洞窟に住み、向かいには渦巻くカリュブディスがいた。船乗りはどちらかを選ばねばならない。オデュッセウスは船全体を失う危険を避け、スキュラのそばを通り、六つの頭に一人ずつ、六人の部下を失った。かつて美しいニンフだったが、魔女の嫉妬で変えられたという話もある。',
'No one can fight Scylla; you can only sail past her quickly. The goddess Circe told Odysseus to row hard and to call on Scylla’s mother, Crataeis, to keep her from striking twice.':'スキュラとは戦えない。素早く通り過ぎるしかない。女神キルケはオデュッセウスに全力で漕ぎ、母クラタイスに祈って二度目の攻撃を防ぐよう告げた。',
'The empusa is a shape-shifting demon sent by the dark goddess Hecate. She has one leg of bronze and one of a donkey, and her hair is on fire. She takes the form of a beautiful woman, a dog or a cow, seduces young men and drinks their blood. In the life of the philosopher Apollonius, a young man was about to marry a lovely bride who was really an empusa, until Apollonius exposed her.':'エンプーサは闇の女神ヘカテーが遣わす変身する悪魔だ。片脚は青銅、もう片脚はロバで、髪は燃えている。美女や犬、牛に化けて若者を誘惑し、血を吸う。哲学者アポロニオスの伝記では、若者が美しい花嫁と結婚しようとしたが、アポロニオスが正体を暴くと彼女はエンプーサだった。',
'Insult an empusa loudly and she flees shrieking: that is how a traveller in Aristophanes’ play drives one off. Her bronze leg rings on stones, and gives her away.':'大声でエンプーサを罵れば、叫びながら逃げる。アリストパネスの劇の旅人はそうして追い払った。石に当たる青銅の脚の音が正体を知らせる。',
'The mapinguari is a giant creature of the Amazon rainforest, covered in thick red fur, with backward-pointing feet and, some say, a single eye and a second mouth in its belly. It smells so terrible that hunters faint, and it screams like a man. Some scientists think the legend might remember the giant ground sloths that once lived in South America, but rubber tappers and hunters still tell stories of meeting one.':'マピンガリはアマゾン熱帯雨林の巨大な怪物で、厚い赤毛に覆われ、足は後ろ向きだ。片目で腹にもう一つ口があるという説もある。臭いがひどく、狩人は気絶し、人のような叫び声をあげる。南米にかつて生息した巨大地上性ナマケモノの記憶が伝説になったと考える科学者もいるが、ゴム採取人や狩人はいまも遭遇談を語る。',
'Its fur is like armour; only the mouth in its belly or the top of its head can be wounded, hunters say. It follows its own trail backwards, so walk the wrong way along its tracks to escape.':'毛皮は鎧のようで、腹の口か頭頂部しか傷つけられないと狩人は言う。自分の足跡を逆にたどるので、跡と反対の向きに進めば逃げられる。',
'The pishtaco is a terrifying figure of the Andes: a tall, pale stranger who hunts lonely travellers on the mountain roads at night, kills them and steals their body fat, which he sells to make candles, church bells or machines. The legend began in colonial times and reflected the people’s fear of foreigners who came to take what was theirs. Even in modern times, rumours of pishtacos have caused panic in Peruvian villages.':'ピシュタコはアンデスの恐ろしい存在で、背が高く青白い見知らぬ男だ。夜の山道で一人旅の者を狩り、殺して体脂肪を奪い、蝋燭や教会の鐘、機械を作るために売る。植民地時代に生まれた伝説は、土地の物を奪いに来る外国人への恐怖を映していた。現代でもピシュタコの噂はペルーの村々に恐慌を起こしている。',
'Never walk the mountain roads alone at night, and be wary of a stranger who offers help on a lonely path.':'夜の山道を一人で歩いてはならない。寂しい道で助けを申し出る見知らぬ者には気をつけよう。',
'The tunche is a dangerous spirit of the Amazon forest that announces itself with a whistle. It is the soul of someone who died a bad death and cannot rest, wandering the paths at night. When you hear its whistle, if you whistle back or answer its call, it will come for you and you will fall sick or die. People in the Peruvian jungle still go silent when they hear a strange whistle in the dark.':'トゥンチェは口笛で存在を知らせるアマゾンの危険な精霊だ。無残な死を遂げて安らげない者の魂で、夜道をさまよう。口笛が聞こえて吹き返したり返事をしたりすると、襲いに来て病や死をもたらす。ペルーのジャングルでは今も、暗闇で奇妙な口笛を聞くと皆が黙り込む。',
'Never whistle back. Stay silent, light tobacco, and stay with others until the whistling moves away.':'決して吹き返してはならない。黙ってタバコに火をつけ、口笛が遠ざかるまで仲間と一緒にいよう。'
});
addLang('zh', {
'The mangas is the great many-headed demon of Mongol and Buryat epics, a cannibal giant with twelve, fifteen or even a hundred heads. He devours whole herds and peoples and steals the wives of heroes. The hero Geser Khan and many epic warriors spend years hunting mangas, who split their souls into animals and objects hidden around the world.':'芒古斯是蒙古和布里亚特史诗中的多头巨魔，拥有十二、十五甚至一百个头，是吃人的巨人。它吞食整个部族和畜群，还掳走英雄的妻子。英雄格萨尔汗和许多史诗勇士花多年追捕它，因为芒古斯把灵魂分藏在世界各地的动物和物品中。',
'A mangas keeps its souls outside its body: in a fish, a bird, a golden box or a wasp. The hero must find and kill every soul, or the demon will rise again.':'芒古斯把灵魂藏在身体之外：鱼、鸟、金盒或黄蜂之中。英雄必须找出并消灭每一个灵魂，否则恶魔会再次复活。',
'The olgoi-khorkhoi, the ‘large intestine worm’, is said to live under the sands of the Gobi desert. It is dark red, as thick as a man’s arm and up to a metre and a half long. Nomads say it can spit acid that eats through metal and kill from a distance with a blast like lightning. It comes out in June and July, after rain, when the ground is wet. Many expeditions have searched for it; none has found it.':'据说“肠虫”奥尔戈伊-霍尔霍伊住在戈壁沙漠的沙下。它呈暗红色，粗如人臂，最长约一米半。游牧民说它会喷出能腐蚀金属的酸液，还能以闪电般的冲击远距离杀人。六月和七月雨后地面潮湿时，它会现身。许多探险队搜寻过，却无人找到。',
'Herders say the death worm is drawn to the colour yellow and that it hates the vibrations of footsteps. Stay off the dunes after summer rain.':'牧民说，死亡之虫会被黄色吸引，而且讨厌脚步的震动。夏雨过后别去沙丘。',
'The Chimera was a fire-breathing monster of Lycia, with the body and head of a lion, a goat’s head rising from its back, and a snake for a tail. It burned the land and ate the flocks. King Iobates sent the young hero Bellerophon to kill it, hoping he would die. But Bellerophon tamed the winged horse Pegasus, flew above the Chimera, and pushed a lump of lead on the end of his spear into its fiery mouth. The lead melted and choked it.':'奇美拉是吕基亚喷火的怪物，长着狮身狮头，背上冒出羊头，尾巴是蛇。它焚烧土地、吞食羊群。伊俄巴忒斯王派年轻英雄柏勒洛丰去杀它，希望他送命。但柏勒洛丰驯服飞马珀伽索斯，飞到奇美拉上方，把枪尖上的铅块刺入它的火口。铅熔化后堵住喉咙，将它窒息。',
'Attack from the air, where its three heads cannot reach you, and use its own fire against it: lead melted in its throat is what killed it.':'从空中攻击，避开三头的攻击范围，并利用它自己的火焰：熔化的铅堵住喉咙，正是这样杀死了它。',
'Scylla was a monster with six long necks, each with a head full of three rows of sharp teeth, and dogs’ heads around her waist. She lived in a cave in the cliffs of a narrow strait, opposite the whirlpool Charybdis. Sailors had to choose between them. Odysseus chose to pass close to Scylla, losing six men, one for each head, rather than risk losing his whole ship to the whirlpool. Some said she was once a beautiful nymph, changed by a witch’s jealousy.':'斯库拉是长着六条长颈的怪物，每个头都有三排利齿，腰间还环绕着狗头。她住在狭窄海峡峭壁的洞穴里，对面是漩涡卡律布狄斯。水手必须二选一。奥德修斯选择贴近斯库拉而行，失去六名同伴，每个头夺走一人，也不冒整艘船被漩涡吞没的风险。有人说她曾是美丽的宁芙，被女巫的嫉妒改变了形态。',
'No one can fight Scylla; you can only sail past her quickly. The goddess Circe told Odysseus to row hard and to call on Scylla’s mother, Crataeis, to keep her from striking twice.':'没人能与斯库拉交战，只能迅速驶过。女神喀耳刻告诉奥德修斯奋力划船，并呼唤斯库拉的母亲克拉泰伊斯，以免她再次袭击。',
'The empusa is a shape-shifting demon sent by the dark goddess Hecate. She has one leg of bronze and one of a donkey, and her hair is on fire. She takes the form of a beautiful woman, a dog or a cow, seduces young men and drinks their blood. In the life of the philosopher Apollonius, a young man was about to marry a lovely bride who was really an empusa, until Apollonius exposed her.':'恩普萨是黑暗女神赫卡忒派出的变形恶魔，一条腿是青铜，另一条是驴腿，头发燃烧着火焰。它会化作美女、狗或牛，诱惑年轻男子并吸他们的血。哲学家阿波罗尼奥斯的传记中，一名青年即将迎娶美丽新娘，阿波罗尼奥斯却揭穿她其实是恩普萨。',
'Insult an empusa loudly and she flees shrieking: that is how a traveller in Aristophanes’ play drives one off. Her bronze leg rings on stones, and gives her away.':'大声辱骂恩普萨，她便尖叫着逃走；阿里斯托芬戏剧中的旅人就是这样赶走她的。她的青铜腿碰到石头会发出声响，暴露身份。',
'The mapinguari is a giant creature of the Amazon rainforest, covered in thick red fur, with backward-pointing feet and, some say, a single eye and a second mouth in its belly. It smells so terrible that hunters faint, and it screams like a man. Some scientists think the legend might remember the giant ground sloths that once lived in South America, but rubber tappers and hunters still tell stories of meeting one.':'马平瓜里是亚马逊雨林中的巨兽，全身长着浓密红毛，双脚朝后；有人说它只有一只眼，腹部还有第二张嘴。它恶臭难闻，猎人会被熏晕，叫声像人。有些科学家认为传说可能源于南美曾经生活的巨型地懒，但采胶工和猎人至今仍讲述遇见它的故事。',
'Its fur is like armour; only the mouth in its belly or the top of its head can be wounded, hunters say. It follows its own trail backwards, so walk the wrong way along its tracks to escape.':'猎人说它的毛皮如同铠甲，只有腹部的嘴或头顶才能受伤。它会倒着沿自身足迹行走，所以沿着脚印的反方向走才能逃脱。',
'The pishtaco is a terrifying figure of the Andes: a tall, pale stranger who hunts lonely travellers on the mountain roads at night, kills them and steals their body fat, which he sells to make candles, church bells or machines. The legend began in colonial times and reflected the people’s fear of foreigners who came to take what was theirs. Even in modern times, rumours of pishtacos have caused panic in Peruvian villages.':'皮什塔科是安第斯山脉的恐怖传说：高大苍白的陌生人，夜里在山路上猎杀独行旅客，偷取他们的体脂，卖去制造蜡烛、教堂钟或机器。传说始于殖民时期，反映了当地人对外来者掠夺财物的恐惧。直到现代，皮什塔科的谣言仍会让秘鲁村庄陷入恐慌。',
'Never walk the mountain roads alone at night, and be wary of a stranger who offers help on a lonely path.':'夜间不要独自走山路，也要提防在荒僻小道上主动帮忙的陌生人。',
'The tunche is a dangerous spirit of the Amazon forest that announces itself with a whistle. It is the soul of someone who died a bad death and cannot rest, wandering the paths at night. When you hear its whistle, if you whistle back or answer its call, it will come for you and you will fall sick or die. People in the Peruvian jungle still go silent when they hear a strange whistle in the dark.':'通切是亚马逊森林中的危险精灵，会用口哨声宣告自己的到来。它是横死后无法安息者的灵魂，夜里游荡在小径上。听到它的口哨若吹回去或回应呼唤，它就会来找你，让你患病或丧命。秘鲁丛林里的人至今听到黑暗中的怪异口哨声仍会噤声。',
'Never whistle back. Stay silent, light tobacco, and stay with others until the whistling moves away.':'千万不要吹回去。保持安静，点燃烟草，并与他人待在一起，直到口哨声远去。'
});
